[2026-06-06 10:44:13] [INFO] [PostToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"f19f2dcd-5cb7-4e25-89c6-4a90c9705548","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\f19f2dcd-5cb7-4e25-89c6-4a90c9705548.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"auto","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore Go test patterns","prompt":"In the project at D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus, I need to understand the existing Go test patterns and structure:\n\n1. List all test files (*_test.go) in the project\n2. Read one or two representative test files to understand the testing patterns (naming, assertions, setup, etc.)\n3. Check how tests are organized (testify? standard library? custom helpers?)\n4. Look at how the proxy is tested (tests/proxy/ or tests/e2e/)\n5. Look at how config resolution is tested if any tests exist for it\n\nGive me:\n- The test framework/conventions used\n- Example test patterns\n- Where new tests should go\n- How the ReverseProxy struct is constructed in tests","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_response":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the project at D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus, I need to understand the existing Go test patterns and structure:\n\n1. List all test files (*_test.go) in the project\n2. Read one or two representative test files to understand the testing patterns (naming, assertions, setup, etc.)\n3. Check how tests are organized (testify? standard library? custom helpers?)\n4. Look at how the proxy is tested (tests/proxy/ or tests/e2e/)\n5. Look at how config resolution is tested if any tests exist for it\n\nGive me:\n- The test framework/conventions used\n- Example test patterns\n- Where new tests should go\n- How the ReverseProxy struct is constructed in tests","agentId":"a7bc836fe211a1636","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nBased on my analysis of the Go test files in the project, here's a comprehensive overview of the testing patterns and structure:\n\n## Test Framework and Conventions\n\n### **1. Testing Framework**\nThe project uses:\n- **Standard Go testing library** (`testing`) - No external testing frameworks like testify\n- **httptest** package for HTTP server testing\n- **JSON fixtures** for test data management\n- **Custom testutil package** for reusable testing utilities\n\n### **2. Test Organization**\n\n```\ntests/\n├── backend/          # API endpoint tests\n├── e2e/             # End-to-end proxy tests\n├── integration/     # Integration tests\n├── proxy/           # Proxy layer unit tests\n├── session/         # Session-related tests\n├── sse/             # Server-sent events tests\n├── trace/           # Trace functionality tests\n├── usage/           # Usage/normalization tests\n└── shell/           # Shell-related tests\n```\n\n### **3. Test Patterns and Conventions**\n\n#### **A. Naming Convention**\n- Files: `*_test.go`\n- Functions: `Test{FunctionName}_{Scenario}` (e.g., `TestGetStatus_WithData`, `TestNonStreamingRequest`)\n\n#### **B. Test Structure Patterns**\n\n1. **Unit Tests** (e.g., `tests/proxy/paths_test.go`):\n   ```go\n   func TestIsAllowedPath(t *testing.T) {\n       tests := []struct {\n           path     string\n           expected bool\n       }{\n           {\"/v1/messages\", true},\n           {\"/admin/config\", false},\n       }\n       \n       for _, tt := range tests {\n           got := proxy.IsAllowedPath(tt.path)\n           if got != tt.expected {\n               t.Errorf(\"IsAllowedPath(%q) = %v, want %v\", tt.path, got, tt.expected)\n           }\n       }\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **API Integration Tests** (e.g., `tests/backend/status_api_test.go`):\n   - Uses test environment setup with `setupStatusTest()`\n   - Creates temporary database files\n   - Tests HTTP handlers with `httptest.NewServer`\n   - Includes helper methods for making requests (`get()`, `post()`)\n   - Uses `t.Cleanup()` for resource cleanup\n\n3. **E2E Tests** (e.g., `tests/e2e/proxy_trace_test.go`):\n   - Uses fixture-based testing with JSON test data\n   - Creates real proxy instances with `proxy.NewReverseProxy()`\n   - Tests actual HTTP request/response flows\n   - Validates trace output and statistics\n\n#### **C. Common Test Helpers**\n\n1. **Environment Setup Pattern**:\n   ```go\n   type statusTestEnv struct {\n       srv   *httptest.Server\n       store *store.SQLiteStore\n   }\n   \n   func setupStatusTest(t *testing.T) *statusTestEnv {\n       t.Helper()\n       \n       // Create temp database\n       f, err := os.CreateTemp(\"\", \"test-*.db\")\n       // ... setup code ...\n       \n       t.Cleanup(func() {\n           // Cleanup code\n       })\n       \n       return &statusTestEnv{srv: srv, store: s}\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **Request/Response Helpers**:\n   ```go\n   func (e *statusTestEnv) get(t *testing.T, path string) *http.Response {\n       resp, err := http.Get(e.srv.URL + path)\n       if err != nil {\n           t.Fatal(err)\n       }\n       return resp\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **JSON Parsing Helpers**:\n   ```go\n   func readStatusResponse(t *testing.T, resp *http.Response) statusResponse {\n       defer resp.Body.Close()\n       b, err := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)\n       // ... parse JSON ...\n   }\n   ```\n\n### **4. Test Data Management**\n\n#### **Fixture System** (`internal/testutil/fixture.go`):\n- JSON files define test scenarios with request/response data\n- Fixture structure:\n  ```go\n  type Fixture struct {\n      Name          string          `json:\"name\"`\n      Request       FixtureRequest  `json:\"request\"`\n      Response      FixtureResponse `json:\"response\"`\n      ExpectedTrace ExpectedTrace   `json:\"expected_trace\"`\n  }\n  ```\n- Auto-searches for `testdata/fixtures/` directory upward\n\n### **5. ReverseProxy Construction in Tests**\n\n#### **A. Basic Proxy Creation**:\n```go\n// From E2E tests\ntraceDir := t.TempDir()\nrp := proxy.NewReverseProxy(mockServer.URL, traceDir)\nport, err := rp.Start(\"127.0.0.1\", 0) // Use random port\n```\n\n#### **B. Proxy with Trace Initialization**:\n```go\n// From e2e_test.go\nfunc setupProxyWithTrace(t *testing.T, mockServerURL string) (string, string) {\n    traceDir := t.TempDir()\n    rp := proxy.NewReverseProxy(mockServerURL, traceDir)\n    port, err := rp.Start(\"127.0.0.1\", 0)\n    \n    // Initialize trace via internal endpoint\n    resp, _ := http.Post(proxyURL+\"/_internal/trace-init\", \n        \"application/json\", \n        strings.NewReader(`{\"session_id\":\"test-session-001\"}`))\n    \n    return proxyURL, tracePath\n}\n```\n\n#### **C. Key Proxy Components in Tests**:\n- **Target URL**: The upstream server URL to proxy to\n- **Trace Directory**: Where to store trace files\n- **Session ID**: For trace tracking\n- **Temporary Ports**: Use port 0 for random available port\n- **Cleanup**: Always call `rp.Stop()` in `t.Cleanup()`\n\n### **6. Where New Tests Should Go**\n\n1. **Unit tests for proxy features**: `tests/proxy/`\n2. **API endpoint tests**: `tests/backend/`\n3. **End-to-end integration tests**: `tests/e2e/`\n4. **Component integration**: `tests/integration/`\n5. **Specific functionality**: \n   - SSE handling: `tests/sse/`\n   - Session management: `tests/session/`\n   - Trace functionality: `tests/trace/`\n\n### **7. Key Testing Patterns to Follow**\n\n1. **Always use `t.Helper()`** in helper functions\n2. **Use `t.Cleanup()`** for resource cleanup\n3. **Create temporary files/directories** with `t.TempDir()`\n4. **Test both positive and negative scenarios**\n5. **Use table-driven tests** for multiple test cases\n6. **Validate HTTP status codes and error responses**\n7. **Check trace output for proxy tests**\n8. **Use fixtures** for complex test data\n\nThe project has a well-structured testing approach that emphasizes integration testing with real HTTP servers and comprehensive trace validation, which is crucial for a proxy system."}],"totalDurationMs":88941,"totalTokens":60354,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":1752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":56317,"output_tokens":2285,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}},"tool_use_id":"call_307faa06c3bb4795854b7e8f","duration_ms":90767}
