[2026-06-06 11:57:49] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"d20ab83c-226b-4225-be31-28c59aa725e9","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\d20ab83c-226b-4225-be31-28c59aa725e9.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"aeb3bc255e528654f","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\d20ab83c-226b-4225-be31-28c59aa725e9\\subagents\\agent-aeb3bc255e528654f.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Now I have a complete picture. Here is my comprehensive analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Analysis of claude_tap_plus Proxy Request Body Handling\n\n### 1. `serveHTTP` Request Body Processing (`reverse.go`)\n\nThe `serveHTTP` method (line 112) processes the request body in this exact sequence:\n\n1. **Read entire body** (line 126-131): `io.ReadAll(r.Body)` captures raw bytes.\n2. **Parse to JSON** (lines 134-137): `json.Unmarshal` into `any` (used later for extracting `model`, `stream`, and building trace records).\n3. **Model rewrite** (line 140): `rewriteModel(bodyBytes, reqBody, p.model)` is the ONLY request body transformation.\n4. **Re-parse after rewrite** (lines 143-146): Re-unmarshal the rewritten bytes.\n5. **Fallback model rewrite** (lines 167-173): If upstream is unavailable AND a fallback config exists with a model, `rewriteModel` runs a second time with the fallback model.\n\n**There are no other request body modifications.** The only transformation is `rewriteModel`. No middleware chain, no pluggable hooks, no other field injection. The body goes to upstream as-is after the optional model swap.\n\n### 2. All Files in `internal/proxy/` -- No Middleware or Additional Transformation Logic\n\nThe proxy directory contains exactly these files:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `reverse.go` | Core proxy: `serveHTTP`, `rewriteModel`, streaming/non-streaming handlers, trace writing, internal endpoints |\n| `headers.go` | Header filtering (hop-by-hop removal), sensitive header redaction for logs, `HeadersToMap` |\n| `netutil.go` | TCP listener creation (type alias for `net.TCPAddr`) |\n| `paths.go` | URL path whitelist (`AllowedPathPrefixes`) |\n| `model_rewrite_test.go` | Tests for model rewrite (contract 3) |\n| `fallback_test.go` | Tests for upstream fallback (contract 4) |\n\n**There is no middleware pattern, no request body interceptor chain, no plugin system.** Everything is procedural within `serveHTTP`.\n\n### 3. `mirrorReasoning()` in `sse/reassembler.go` (Response-Side, Not Request-Side)\n\n`mirrorReasoning` (lines 388-399) operates on the **response** SSE reassembly snapshot, NOT on request bodies. It handles the OpenAI Chat Completions streaming format where `reasoning_content` arrives as a field in `choices[0].delta`:\n\n**How it works:**\n1. During `accumulateChatCompletionChunk` (line 306-309), when a `delta` contains `reasoning_content`, it accumulates the text into `msg[\"reasoning_content\"]` and then calls `r.mirrorReasoning(...)`.\n2. `mirrorReasoning` scans the snapshot's `content` array for an existing block with `type: \"thinking\"`.\n3. If found, it updates that block's `thinking` field with the full accumulated reasoning string.\n4. If NOT found, it **prepends** a new `{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"thinking\": reasoning}` block at index 0 of the content array.\n\nThis is purely for trace/reassembly purposes -- it converts OpenAI-format `reasoning_content` into Anthropic-format `thinking` content blocks so the reconstructed snapshot is compatible with the Anthropic schema. **This does not modify any request body and does not affect what gets sent upstream.**\n\nThe `thinking_delta` case (line 193-194) handles native Anthropic SSE streaming of thinking content, accumulating `delta.thinking` into `block[\"thinking\"]`.\n\n### 4. Config Files -- No Thinking-Related Configuration\n\nAfter searching the entire `claude_tap_plus` codebase for `thinking`, `budget_tokens`, `extended_thinking`, and `thinking_mode`, there is **zero thinking-related config**. The config system covers:\n\n- **`client.go`**: Defines `ClientConfig` with `Cmd`, `BaseURLEnv`, `DefaultTarget`, etc. -- no thinking fields.\n- **`profiles.go`**: `ProfileConfig` has `BaseURL`, `APIKey`, `AuthToken`, `Provider`, `Model` -- no thinking fields.\n- **`resolve.go`**: `ResolvedConfig` has `BaseURL`, `APIKey`, `AuthToken`, `Model` -- no thinking fields.\n- **`claudeconfig.go`**: Reads `~/.claude.json` for `base_url`, `model`, and env vars -- no thinking fields.\n\nThe config resolution priority chain is: CLI args > profiles.json > environment variables > `~/.claude.json` > defaults. None of these levels include any thinking/extended thinking parameters.\n\n### 5. `main.go` -- Proxy Configuration and Startup\n\nThe `runProxy` function (line 114) wires everything together:\n\n1. Parses `--tap-*` flags (target, port, output-dir, verbose, console, profile, api-key, auth-token, base-url).\n2. Calls `config.ResolveTargetConfig(...)` to resolve the upstream target and model.\n3. Creates `proxy.NewReverseProxy(target, tapOutputDir)`.\n4. Calls `rp.SetModel(resolved.Model)` -- this is the only model-level configuration that drives request body rewriting.\n5. Calls `loadFallbackConfig()` which reads `~/.claude/settings.json` for fallback base_url/model/auth.\n6. Calls `rp.SetFallbackConfig(fallback)`.\n7. Starts the proxy, registers with backend, launches Claude Code as a child process.\n\nThere is no hook point for injecting additional request body transformations between parsing and forwarding.\n\n### Summary: Existing Transformation Infrastructure\n\n**What transformations exist:**\n- `rewriteModel()`: The sole request body transformation. Swaps/injects the `model` field in JSON bodies.\n\n**What infrastructure exists for adding new transformations:**\n- The request body is already fully read into `[]byte` and parsed into `any` before forwarding (lines 126-146), so there is a natural insertion point between the parse and the `http.NewRequest` call (line 181).\n- The pattern used by `rewriteModel` -- take `[]byte` + parsed `any`, return modified `[]byte` -- is a clean template for additional transformation functions.\n- There is no middleware framework, no hook system, no plugin architecture. Adding a new transformation would mean adding a new function call in the `serveHTTP` method, similar to how `rewriteModel` is called.\n\n**Key files for adding request body transformations:**\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` -- the `serveHTTP` method (around lines 140-180) is where new body transforms would be inserted.\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/config/resolve.go` -- if thinking config needs to be added to the resolution chain.\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/config/profiles.go` -- if `ProfileConfig` needs new thinking-related fields.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
