[2026-06-06 12:00:21] [INFO] [PostToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"d20ab83c-226b-4225-be31-28c59aa725e9","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\d20ab83c-226b-4225-be31-28c59aa725e9.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Design thinking fix plan","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for fixing a 400 API error in the claude_tap_plus proxy.\n\n## Problem\nThe user is using 智谱AI's Anthropic-compatible endpoint (`https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/anthropic`) with thinking/extended thinking enabled. The proxy at `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` passes request bodies through to upstream with only `model` field rewriting.\n\nWhen thinking mode is enabled, 智谱's API requires ALL assistant messages in the conversation history to include `reasoning_content`. But Claude Code's tool-call assistant messages don't include this field. This causes:\n```\n400 thinking is enabled but reasoning_content is missing in assistant tool call message at index 12\n```\n\n## Current Architecture\nThe proxy's `serveHTTP` method in `reverse.go`:\n1. Reads request body into `[]byte` and parses to `any`\n2. Calls `rewriteModel(bodyBytes, reqBody, p.model)` - the ONLY body transformation\n3. Forwards to upstream\n\n`rewriteModel` pattern: takes `(body []byte, parsed any, model string) []byte` - marshals modified JSON back to bytes.\n\nThe SSE reassembler already handles `reasoning_content` in RESPONSES (line 306-308 of reassembler.go) - it mirrors it into thinking blocks. But this is response-side only.\n\n## Key Files\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` - where the fix goes\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/model_rewrite_test.go` - test pattern to follow\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/sse/reassembler.go` - existing reasoning_content handling (response side)\n\n## Constraints\n- Follow existing patterns (rewriteModel style)\n- Don't break non-thinking mode requests\n- Must handle both: `content` as array (Anthropic format) and potentially `reasoning_content` as top-level field\n- The proxy should only inject when thinking mode is detected in the request\n\n## Design Requirements\n1. New function: detect if thinking is enabled in the request (look for `thinking` field in body)\n2. If thinking enabled, iterate `messages` array, find assistant messages with tool_use blocks but missing thinking content\n3. For those messages, inject a minimal thinking block into the content array\n4. Add the function call in `serveHTTP` after `rewriteModel`\n5. Add tests following the `model_rewrite_test.go` pattern\n\nPlease provide a detailed implementation plan with exact code locations and the function signature.","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_response":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for fixing a 400 API error in the claude_tap_plus proxy.\n\n## Problem\nThe user is using 智谱AI's Anthropic-compatible endpoint (`https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/anthropic`) with thinking/extended thinking enabled. The proxy at `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` passes request bodies through to upstream with only `model` field rewriting.\n\nWhen thinking mode is enabled, 智谱's API requires ALL assistant messages in the conversation history to include `reasoning_content`. But Claude Code's tool-call assistant messages don't include this field. This causes:\n```\n400 thinking is enabled but reasoning_content is missing in assistant tool call message at index 12\n```\n\n## Current Architecture\nThe proxy's `serveHTTP` method in `reverse.go`:\n1. Reads request body into `[]byte` and parses to `any`\n2. Calls `rewriteModel(bodyBytes, reqBody, p.model)` - the ONLY body transformation\n3. Forwards to upstream\n\n`rewriteModel` pattern: takes `(body []byte, parsed any, model string) []byte` - marshals modified JSON back to bytes.\n\nThe SSE reassembler already handles `reasoning_content` in RESPONSES (line 306-308 of reassembler.go) - it mirrors it into thinking blocks. But this is response-side only.\n\n## Key Files\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` - where the fix goes\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/model_rewrite_test.go` - test pattern to follow\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/sse/reassembler.go` - existing reasoning_content handling (response side)\n\n## Constraints\n- Follow existing patterns (rewriteModel style)\n- Don't break non-thinking mode requests\n- Must handle both: `content` as array (Anthropic format) and potentially `reasoning_content` as top-level field\n- The proxy should only inject when thinking mode is detected in the request\n\n## Design Requirements\n1. New function: detect if thinking is enabled in the request (look for `thinking` field in body)\n2. If thinking enabled, iterate `messages` array, find assistant messages with tool_use blocks but missing thinking content\n3. For those messages, inject a minimal thinking block into the content array\n4. Add the function call in `serveHTTP` after `rewriteModel`\n5. Add tests following the `model_rewrite_test.go` pattern\n\nPlease provide a detailed implementation plan with exact code locations and the function signature.","agentId":"a6d36c1dccf4e38ad","agentType":"Plan","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have complete understanding of the codebase. Let me write the detailed implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Fix 400 API Error for Thinking Mode with Tool-Call Messages\n\n### Problem Analysis\n\nWhen Claude Code sends requests through the proxy to ZhiPu AI's Anthropic-compatible endpoint with thinking mode enabled, assistant messages that contain `tool_use` blocks lack `reasoning_content` (or a thinking content block). ZhiPu's API strictly validates that every assistant message in the conversation history must include `reasoning_content` when thinking is enabled. The current proxy passes request bodies through without modification (other than model rewriting), so this validation failure reaches upstream and causes a 400 error:\n\n```\n400 thinking is enabled but reasoning_content is missing in assistant tool call message at index 12\n```\n\n### Understanding the Anthropic Messages API Request Structure\n\nIn the Anthropic Messages API, when thinking is enabled:\n\n- The request body contains a top-level `thinking` field (e.g., `{\"type\": \"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\": 10000}`).\n- Assistant messages in the `messages` array have `content` as an array of content blocks.\n- A well-formed assistant message with thinking includes a `thinking` block as the first element in the content array, followed by `text` and/or `tool_use` blocks.\n- Claude Code's tool-call assistant messages omit the thinking block entirely -- they contain only `tool_use` blocks (and optionally a `text` block).\n\nThe fix must inject a minimal `thinking` content block into assistant messages that have `tool_use` blocks but are missing thinking content, but only when the request has thinking mode enabled.\n\n### Design: Following the Existing `rewriteModel` Pattern\n\nThe existing `rewriteModel` function follows a clear contract:\n\n```go\nfunc rewriteModel(body []byte, parsed any, model string) []byte\n```\n\nIt takes raw bytes + parsed `any`, modifies the parsed map, marshals back to bytes. The new function will follow this same signature pattern.\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n\n---\n\n#### Step 1: Add `injectThinkingContent` function to `reverse.go`\n\n**Location**: `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`, after the existing `rewriteModel` function (after line 616).\n\n**Function signature**:\n\n```go\n// injectThinkingContent 在启用 thinking 模式时，为缺少 reasoning_content 的 assistant tool_call 消息注入最简 thinking 内容块。\n//\n// 智谱AI 的 Anthropic 兼容端点要求：当 thinking 启用时，所有 assistant 消息必须包含 reasoning_content。\n// Claude Code 的 tool_call 消息不包含此字段，导致上游 400 错误。\n//\n// 此函数检测请求中的 thinking 配置，仅在 thinking 启用时执行注入，\n// 不会影响非 thinking 模式的请求。\nfunc injectThinkingContent(body []byte, parsed any) []byte\n```\n\n**Implementation logic**:\n\n```go\nfunc injectThinkingContent(body []byte, parsed any) []byte {\n    if len(body) == 0 {\n        return body\n    }\n\n    m, ok := parsed.(map[string]any)\n    if !ok {\n        return body\n    }\n\n    // 1. Detect if thinking is enabled\n    thinking, ok := m[\"thinking\"].(map[string]any)\n    if !ok {\n        return body // no thinking field, pass through\n    }\n    thinkingType, _ := thinking[\"type\"].(string)\n    if thinkingType != \"enabled\" {\n        return body // thinking not enabled, pass through\n    }\n\n    // 2. Get messages array\n    messages, ok := m[\"messages\"].([]any)\n    if !ok || len(messages) == 0 {\n        return body\n    }\n\n    modified := false\n    for i, msgRaw := range messages {\n        msg, ok := msgRaw.(map[string]any)\n        if !ok {\n            continue\n        }\n\n        // Only process assistant messages\n        role, _ := msg[\"role\"].(string)\n        if role != \"assistant\" {\n            continue\n        }\n\n        // Check if content is an array\n        content, ok := msg[\"content\"].([]any)\n        if !ok || len(content) == 0 {\n            continue\n        }\n\n        // Check if this message has tool_use blocks\n        hasToolUse := false\n        hasThinking := false\n        for _, blockRaw := range content {\n            block, ok := blockRaw.(map[string]any)\n            if !ok {\n                continue\n            }\n            blockType, _ := block[\"type\"].(string)\n            if blockType == \"tool_use\" {\n                hasToolUse = true\n            }\n            if blockType == \"thinking\" {\n                hasThinking = true\n            }\n        }\n\n        // If has tool_use but no thinking block, inject one\n        if hasToolUse && !hasThinking {\n            thinkingBlock := map[string]any{\n                \"type\": \"thinking\",\n                \"thinking\": \"\",\n            }\n            // Insert at the beginning of content array\n            newContent := make([]any, 0, len(content)+1)\n            newContent = append(newContent, thinkingBlock)\n            newContent = append(newContent, content...)\n            msg[\"content\"] = newContent\n            messages[i] = msg\n            modified = true\n        }\n    }\n\n    if !modified {\n        return body\n    }\n\n    m[\"messages\"] = messages\n    rewritten, err := json.Marshal(m)\n    if err != nil {\n        return body\n    }\n    return rewritten\n}\n```\n\n**Key design decisions**:\n\n1. **Empty string `thinking` value**: The injected thinking block uses `thinking: \"\"` (empty string). This is the minimal valid value that satisfies ZhiPu's validation. The API does not validate the content richness of the thinking block -- it only checks for its presence.\n\n2. **Prepend to content array**: The thinking block is inserted as the first element of the content array, matching Anthropic's convention where thinking always precedes text and tool_use blocks.\n\n3. **Only injects when `hasToolUse && !hasThinking`**: Pure text assistant messages might already have thinking blocks from prior responses. Tool-call messages from Claude Code are the specific gap.\n\n4. **Early returns**: If thinking is not enabled, if the body is not JSON, or if no modifications are needed, the original bytes are returned unchanged. This ensures zero impact on non-thinking requests.\n\n---\n\n#### Step 2: Wire the function into `serveHTTP`\n\n**Location**: `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`, lines 139-146.\n\n**Current code** (lines 139-146):\n\n```go\n// 请求体 model 改写（契约 3）\nbodyBytes = rewriteModel(bodyBytes, reqBody, p.model)\n\n// 重新解析改写后的请求体\nreqBody = nil\nif len(bodyBytes) > 0 {\n    _ = json.Unmarshal(bodyBytes, &reqBody)\n}\n```\n\n**New code** (insert after line 146, before the reqID generation at line 148):\n\n```go\n// 请求体 model 改写（契约 3）\nbodyBytes = rewriteModel(bodyBytes, reqBody, p.model)\n\n// 重新解析改写后的请求体\nreqBody = nil\nif len(bodyBytes) > 0 {\n    _ = json.Unmarshal(bodyBytes, &reqBody)\n}\n\n// 为 thinking 模式下的 assistant tool_call 消息注入 reasoning_content\nbodyBytes = injectThinkingContent(bodyBytes, reqBody)\n\n// 重新解析注入后的请求体\nreqBody = nil\nif len(bodyBytes) > 0 {\n    _ = json.Unmarshal(bodyBytes, &reqBody)\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the exact same pattern as `rewriteModel`: call the function, then re-parse the result. The re-parse is needed because downstream code (building the upstream request, trace logging) uses the parsed `reqBody`.\n\n**Important**: The `injectThinkingContent` call must happen AFTER `rewriteModel` and its re-parse, so it operates on the already-model-rewritten body. This ensures the final `bodyBytes` and `reqBody` reflect both transformations.\n\n---\n\n#### Step 3: Add tests following `model_rewrite_test.go` pattern\n\n**Location**: Create new file `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/thinking_inject_test.go`\n\n**Test cases** (following the table-driven test pattern from `model_rewrite_test.go`):\n\n```go\npackage proxy\n\nimport (\n    \"bytes\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"net/http\"\n    \"net/http/httptest\"\n    \"testing\"\n)\n```\n\n**Test 1**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_ToolCallMessage` -- thinking enabled + assistant message with tool_use and no thinking block. Verifies thinking block is injected.\n\n**Test 2**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_NoThinkingConfig` -- no `thinking` field in request. Verifies body passes through unchanged.\n\n**Test 3**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_ThinkingDisabled` -- `thinking.type = \"disabled\"`. Verifies body passes through unchanged.\n\n**Test 4**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_AlreadyHasThinking` -- assistant message already has thinking block. Verifies no duplicate injection.\n\n**Test 5**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_MixedMessages` -- conversation with user messages, assistant text messages (with thinking), and assistant tool-call messages (without thinking). Verifies only the tool-call messages get injected.\n\n**Test 6**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_NonThinkingRequestUnchanged` -- full request without thinking field, verifies all fields preserved identically (similar to `TestRequestBodyRewrite_OtherFieldsUnchanged`).\n\n**Test 7**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_EmptyBody` -- empty body, returns unchanged.\n\n**Test 8**: `TestInjectThinkingContent_NonJSONBody` -- non-JSON body, returns unchanged.\n\nEach test follows the same integration pattern used in `model_rewrite_test.go`: create a mock upstream server with `httptest.NewServer`, create a proxy pointing to it, send a request through the proxy, and inspect what the upstream received.\n\n**Example test structure** (Test 1):\n\n```go\nfunc TestInjectThinkingContent_ToolCallMessage(t *testing.T) {\n    var capturedBody []byte\n    mockUpstream := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n        capturedBody, _ = io.ReadAll(r.Body)\n        w.Header().Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n        w.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n        w.Write([]byte(`{\"id\":\"msg_test\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[],\"model\":\"test\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}}`))\n    }))\n    defer mockUpstream.Close()\n\n    traceDir := t.TempDir()\n    rp := NewReverseProxy(mockUpstream.URL, traceDir)\n    rp.model = \"test-model\"\n\n    _, err := rp.Start(\"127.0.0.1\", 0)\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"start proxy: %v\", err)\n    }\n    defer rp.Stop()\n\n    // Request with thinking enabled and assistant tool_call message missing thinking\n    reqBody := map[string]any{\n        \"model\":  \"test-model\",\n        \"stream\": true,\n        \"thinking\": map[string]any{\n            \"type\":          \"enabled\",\n            \"budget_tokens\": 10000,\n        },\n        \"messages\": []any{\n            map[string]any{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"read the file\"},\n            map[string]any{\n                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                \"content\": []any{\n                    map[string]any{\n                        \"type\": \"tool_use\",\n                        \"id\":   \"toolu_123\",\n                        \"name\": \"Read\",\n                        \"input\": map[string]any{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/test.txt\"},\n                    },\n                },\n            },\n            map[string]any{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": []any{map[string]any{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_123\", \"content\": \"file contents\"}}},\n        },\n    }\n    bodyBytes, _ := json.Marshal(reqBody)\n\n    req, _ := http.NewRequest(\"POST\", rp.URL()+\"/v1/messages\", bytes.NewReader(bodyBytes))\n    req.Header.Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n\n    resp, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"send request: %v\", err)\n    }\n    resp.Body.Close()\n\n    // Verify upstream received the injected thinking block\n    var upstreamBody map[string]any\n    if err := json.Unmarshal(capturedBody, &upstreamBody); err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"parse upstream body: %v\", err)\n    }\n\n    messages := upstreamBody[\"messages\"].([]any)\n    assistantMsg := messages[1].(map[string]any)\n    content := assistantMsg[\"content\"].([]any)\n\n    if len(content) != 2 {\n        t.Fatalf(\"assistant content blocks = %d, want 2\", len(content))\n    }\n\n    firstBlock := content[0].(map[string]any)\n    if firstBlock[\"type\"] != \"thinking\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"first content block type = %q, want %q\", firstBlock[\"type\"], \"thinking\")\n    }\n    if thinking, ok := firstBlock[\"thinking\"].(string); !ok || thinking != \"\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"thinking value = %q, want empty string\", firstBlock[\"thinking\"])\n    }\n\n    // Original tool_use block should still be there\n    secondBlock := content[1].(map[string]any)\n    if secondBlock[\"type\"] != \"tool_use\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"second content block type = %q, want %q\", secondBlock[\"type\"], \"tool_use\")\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Step 4: Unit tests for `injectThinkingContent` in isolation\n\nIn addition to the integration tests above, add direct unit tests for the `injectThinkingContent` function itself (similar to how `rewriteModel` could be unit-tested directly). These go in the same test file.\n\n```go\nfunc TestInjectThinkingContent_Unit(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name     string\n        reqBody  string\n        wantSame bool // if true, output should equal input\n        wantLen  int  // expected content array length for the target assistant msg\n    }{\n        {\n            name:     \"no thinking field - passthrough\",\n            reqBody:  `{\"model\":\"x\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"t1\",\"name\":\"n\",\"input\":{}}]}]}`,\n            wantSame: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"thinking disabled - passthrough\",\n            reqBody:  `{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"disabled\"},\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"t1\",\"name\":\"n\",\"input\":{}}]}]}`,\n            wantSame: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"thinking enabled with tool_use - inject\",\n            reqBody:  `{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"enabled\",\"budget_tokens\":10000},\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"t1\",\"name\":\"n\",\"input\":{}}]}]}`,\n            wantSame: false,\n            wantLen:  2,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"thinking enabled but already has thinking - passthrough\",\n            reqBody:  `{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"enabled\"},\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"reasoning\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"t1\",\"name\":\"n\",\"input\":{}}]}]}`,\n            wantSame: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"empty body - passthrough\",\n            reqBody:  \"\",\n            wantSame: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"non-JSON - passthrough\",\n            reqBody:  \"not json\",\n            wantSame: true,\n        },\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            var parsed any\n            if tt.reqBody != \"\" {\n                _ = json.Unmarshal([]byte(tt.reqBody), &parsed)\n            }\n            result := injectThinkingContent([]byte(tt.reqBody), parsed)\n            if tt.wantSame {\n                if string(result) != tt.reqBody {\n                    t.Errorf(\"expected passthrough, got different output\")\n                }\n            } else {\n                var m map[string]any\n                if err := json.Unmarshal(result, &m); err != nil {\n                    t.Fatalf(\"result is not valid JSON: %v\", err)\n                }\n                msgs := m[\"messages\"].([]any)\n                content := msgs[0].(map[string]any)[\"content\"].([]any)\n                if len(content) != tt.wantLen {\n                    t.Errorf(\"content length = %d, want %d\", len(content), tt.wantLen)\n                }\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n| File | Action | Description |\n|------|--------|-------------|\n| `internal/proxy/reverse.go` | Modify | Add `injectThinkingContent` function after line 616. Add call + re-parse block after line 146 in `serveHTTP`. |\n| `internal/proxy/thinking_inject_test.go` | Create | New test file with integration tests and unit tests. |\n\n### Potential Risks and Mitigations\n\n1. **Risk: Breaking non-thinking requests.** Mitigation: The function has early returns for every non-thinking scenario (no `thinking` field, `type != \"enabled\"`, no messages, no tool_use blocks). The `modified` flag prevents unnecessary re-marshal.\n\n2. **Risk: Injecting thinking into messages that intentionally omit it.** Mitigation: Only injects when `hasToolUse && !hasThinking`. Messages that already have thinking blocks are left alone.\n\n3. **Risk: ZhiPu rejecting empty thinking content.** Mitigation: The empty string value `\"\"` should pass ZhiPu's validation since the check is specifically for the presence of `reasoning_content`, not its content. If ZhiPu requires non-empty content, a placeholder like `\".\"` can be used instead.\n\n4. **Risk: Performance impact from extra marshal/unmarshal.** Mitigation: Same pattern as `rewriteModel` -- only re-marshals when modification occurs. No impact on the common (non-thinking) path.\n\n5. **Risk: JSON key ordering changes.** Mitigation: This is inherent to the `map[string]any` + `json.Marshal` approach, already used by `rewriteModel`. ZhiPu's API does not depend on key ordering.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` -- Core file to modify: add `injectThinkingContent` function and wire it into `serveHTTP`\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/model_rewrite_test.go` -- Reference pattern for test structure (table-driven, mock upstream, integration style)\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/sse/reassembler.go` -- Reference for how `reasoning_content` / thinking blocks are handled on the response side (lines 306-308, `mirrorReasoning` function)\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/thinking_inject_test.go` -- New test file to create"}],"totalDurationMs":103980,"totalTokens":54707,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":663,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":49856,"output_tokens":4188,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":9,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":1}},"tool_use_id":"call_a91b026598e748f3a3662c9a","duration_ms":103980}
