ay lacks a `thinking` block, inserts one (`{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\"}`) at the beginning.\n   - **Patch 2:** If the message lacks a top-level `reasoning_content` field, injects it as an empty string.\n\nThe proxy then forwards the modified request to the upstream Kimi API and streams the response back.\n\n**Configuration:** Defaults to listening on `:9090` and forwarding to `https://api.kimi.com/coding`. Both are overridable via `--listen` and `--target` flags.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The integrated thinking injection in the main proxy (`internal/proxy/reverse.go`)\n\nThe main `ReverseProxy` (used by `claude-tap-plus`) includes an **identical but generalized** version of this fix in `injectThinkingContent`. The key difference:\n\n- The standalone kimi-proxy checks for `thinking.type == \"enabled\"` first.\n- The integrated version does **not** check for thinking being enabled -- it **unconditionally** injects for any assistant message containing `tool_use` that is missing the fields. The comment explains: \"empty string is harmless but prevents Kimi from erroring.\"\n\nThis function is called in the main `serveHTTP` flow at line 149, and also re-applied after fallback model rewriting at line 182.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How the proxy determines the upstream provider\n\nThe upstream provider resolution follows a strict priority chain, implemented in `internal/config/resolve.go` (`ResolveTargetConfig`):\n\n| Priority | Source | Config field |\n|----------|--------|--------------|\n| 1 (highest) | CLI flags: `--tap-base-url`, `--tap-api-key`, `--tap-auth-token` | `cliBaseURL`, `cliAPIKey`, `cliAuthToken` |\n| 2 | Named profile from `--tap-profile` (reads `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`) | `ProfileConfig.BaseURL`, `.APIKey`, `.AuthToken`, `.Model` |\n| 3 | Environment variables: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | env vars |\n| 4 | `~/.claude.json` (Claude Code's own config) | `base_url`, `model` |\n| 5 (lowest) | Default: `https://api.anthropic.com` | `ClientConfig.DefaultTarget` |\n\nA user targets Kimi by setting `--tap-base-url https://api.kimi.com/coding` or by configuring a profile in `profiles.json` with `\"base_url\": \"https://api.kimi.com/coding\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. FallbackConfig mechanism\n\nThe fallback system provides a safety net when the primary upstream fails:\n\n- **Source of fallback config:** `~/.claude/settings.json` -- the `loadFallbackConfig` function in `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` reads `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, `env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `env.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `model` from it.\n- **Trigger:** When the primary upstream returns a connection error or an HTTP status >= 400, `markUnavailable()` is called (line 593-600 of `reverse.go`). This sets `upstreamAvailable = false` **permanently for the process lifetime** (no recovery).\n- **Behavior after trigger:** All subsequent requests are routed to the fallback `BaseURL`, the model is rewritten to the fallback `Model`, and auth headers are replaced with the fallback credentials.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Kimi-specific path in the whitelist\n\nIn `internal/proxy/paths.go`, the allowed path prefixes include:\n\n```go\n// Kimi API\n\"/coding/v1/\",\n```\n\nThis means requests to paths like `/coding/v1/messages` are allowed through the proxy, matching Kimi's API path structure.\n\n---\n\n## 6. SSE stream handling for Kimi\n\nThe test file `tests/sse/reassembler_test.go` confirms the SSE reassembler handles Kimi-specific stream features:\n\n- **Kimi model in responses:** Tests use `model: \"kimi-k2\"` and `id: \"c_kimi\"`.\n- **`reasoning_content` accumulation:** Kimi sends `reasoning_content` as a field in streaming deltas, which the reassembler accumulates across chunks (e.g., \"Think \" + \"carefully.\" = \"Think carefully.\").\n- **`cached_tokens` extraction:** Kimi's usage response includes `cached_tokens`, which is normalized to `cache_read_input_tokens` in the unified trace format.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThere are two ways to use the Kimi proxy:\n\n1. **Standalone** (`kimi-proxy` binary): A lightweight proxy that only does the `reasoning_content` injection. Run it separately and point Claude Code at it.\n\n2. **Integrated** (`claude-tap-plus` in default proxy mode): The full proxy includes the same thinking injection (generalized to apply unconditionally), plus tracing, fallback, model rewriting, and SSE handling. Configure it to target Kimi via `--tap-base-url https://api.kimi.com/coding` or a profiles.json entry."}],"totalDurationMs":85257,"totalTokens":69140,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":3259,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":64256,"output_tokens":1625,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":14,"searchCount":7,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}},"tool_use_id":"call_9be22eaf7484436da8f21ff4","duration_ms":85257}
