[2026-06-06 13:28:07] [INFO] [PostToolBatch] Input: {"session_id":"ddd6a79e-7998-46d8-ad44-674e2fb35f8e","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\ddd6a79e-7998-46d8-ad44-674e2fb35f8e.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolBatch","tool_calls":[{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore injectThinkingContent","prompt":"In the project at D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus, I need to understand the existing `injectThinkingContent` function and all related thinking/reasoning content handling code.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. Read the full `injectThinkingContent` function in `internal/proxy/reverse.go` - understand what it does, its parameters, return value\n2. Find any tests for this function (check `internal/proxy/*_test.go` files)\n3. Check if there's any reasoning_content caching mechanism already in the codebase\n4. Look for any \"thinking\" or \"reasoning\" related code across the entire `claude_tap_plus` directory\n\nBe thorough - read the complete function implementations, not just signatures.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_125047e59c28416e8be2f3f5","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive picture. Here is my full report.\n\n---\n\n## Thinking/Reasoning Content Handling -- Complete Analysis\n\n### 1. `injectThinkingContent` Function (main implementation)\n\n**File:** `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` (lines 632-738)\n\n**Signature:** `func injectThinkingContent(body []byte, parsed any) []byte`\n\n**Purpose:** Patches outgoing API request bodies to inject missing `reasoning_content` fields and `thinking` content blocks into assistant messages that contain `tool_use` blocks. This is needed because Kimi and similar Anthropic-compatible endpoints reject requests with the error:\n\n> `400 thinking is enabled but reasoning_content is missing in assistant tool call message at index N`\n\n**Algorithm (step by step):**\n\n1. Returns `body` unchanged if empty, non-JSON, or non-object.\n2. Extracts the `messages` array from the parsed JSON. Returns early if absent or empty.\n3. Iterates over each message, filtering for `role == \"assistant\"` only.\n4. For each assistant message with a `content` array, scans all content blocks to determine:\n   - `hasToolUse` -- whether any block has `type == \"tool_use\"`\n   - `hasThinking` -- whether any block has `type == \"thinking\"`\n   - `hasReasoningContent` -- whether the message has a top-level `reasoning_content` field\n5. Skips messages that have no `tool_use` block.\n6. Applies two patches if needed:\n   - **Patch 1:** If no `thinking` block exists, prepends `{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\"}` to the `content` array.\n   - **Patch 2:** If no `reasoning_content` field exists, sets `msg[\"reasoning_content\"] = \"\"` (empty string).\n7. If any modifications were made, re-marshals the entire JSON and returns the new bytes; otherwise returns the original `body` unchanged.\n\n**Called from two places in `serveHTTP()`** (lines 149 and 182):\n- Once after the initial model rewrite.\n- Once again after fallback model rewrite (when upstream is unavailable and fallback is active).\n\n### 2. Tests for `injectThinkingContent`\n\n**File:** `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/thinking_inject_test.go`\n\nThree test functions:\n\n| Test | What it covers |\n|------|---------------|\n| `TestInjectThinkingContent_Unit` | 7 table-driven sub-cases: passthrough for no-tool-use, injection for tool_use without thinking, passthrough when already has thinking+reasoning_content, empty body, non-JSON, JSON array, pure user messages. |\n| `TestInjectThinkingContent_MixedMessages` | A 6-message conversation with user/assistant/tool_result. Verifies only the tool_call assistant messages get injected, text-only assistant messages are left alone, and messages that already have thinking blocks are not duplicated. |\n| `TestInjectThinkingContent_Integration` | Full proxy integration test. Spins up a mock upstream server and a real `ReverseProxy`, sends a request with tool_call messages, and verifies the upstream received the injected `thinking` block (first in content array) and `reasoning_content` field (empty string). |\n\n### 3. Reasoning Content Caching Mechanism\n\n**There is NO caching mechanism for reasoning_content.** The `injectThinkingContent` function always injects an empty string `\"\"` for `reasoning_content` and an empty string `\"\"` for the `thinking` block's `thinking` field. It does not attempt to:\n- Cache previous reasoning_content from earlier turns\n- Store or retrieve any actual thinking content\n- Match reasoning to specific tool calls\n\nThe word \"cache\" appears in the codebase exclusively in the context of **token usage caching** (cache_read_input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cached_tokens), which is about Anthropic's prompt caching feature for token billing, not about reasoning content.\n\n### 4. All Thinking/Reasoning Related Code Across the Codebase\n\nSix files contain thinking/reasoning logic:\n\n**(A) Request-side injection (outgoing requests):**\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n  - `injectThinkingContent()` -- main proxy injection (lines 632-738)\n  - Called in `serveHTTP()` at lines 149 and 182\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/cmd/kimi-proxy/main.go`\n  - `injectReasoningContent()` -- a standalone version of the same logic (lines 120-223). This is a simpler, earlier version that also checks `thinking.type == \"enabled\"` before patching (the proxy version in `reverse.go` does NOT check this -- it patches unconditionally for any tool_use message). Both do the same two patches (thinking block + reasoning_content field).\n\n**(B) Response-side SSE reassembly (incoming responses):**\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n  - `mirrorReasoning()` (lines 390-400) -- Syncs `reasoning_content` into a `thinking` block in the content array during SSE stream reconstruction for OpenAI Chat Completions format.\n  - `accumulateChatCompletionChunk()` (lines 260-372) -- Accumulates `reasoning_content` from streaming delta chunks (line 306-308) and calls `mirrorReasoning()`.\n  - `accumulate()` -- Handles `thinking_delta` SSE event type (line 193-194), appending to `block[\"thinking\"]`.\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/sse/types.go`\n  - `AnthropicContentBlock` struct -- has `Thinking string` field and `Signature string` field for thinking blocks.\n\n**(C) Tests:**\n\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/thinking_inject_test.go` -- Tests for the injection function.\n- `D:/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/claude_tap_plus/tests/sse/reassembler_test.go` -- Contains `TestChatCompletionsReasoningContent` (lines 149-179) and `TestAnthropicThinkingBlock` (lines 340-380) for SSE reassembly.\n\n### Key Architectural Observation\n\nThere are **two implementations** of the reasoning injection logic that differ slightly:\n\n| Aspect | `reverse.go` (proxy) | `kimi-proxy/main.go` (standalone) |\n|--------|---------------------|-------------------------------------|\n| Function name | `injectThinkingContent` | `injectReasoningContent` |\n| Checks `thinking.type == \"enabled\"` | No (patches unconditionally) | Yes (only patches if thinking enabled) |\n| Takes pre-parsed JSON | Yes (second `parsed any` param) | No (parses internally) |\n| Same patches | Yes (thinking block + reasoning_content) | Yes (thinking block + reasoning_content) |\n\nThe unconditional patching in `reverse.go` is deliberate -- the comment says \"empty string is harmless but prevents Kimi errors.\""}]},{"tool_n