[2026-06-06 13:29:14] [INFO] [PreToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"ddd6a79e-7998-46d8-ad44-674e2fb35f8e","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\ddd6a79e-7998-46d8-ad44-674e2fb35f8e.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Design reasoning cache plan","prompt":"I need to design an implementation plan for adding reasoning_content caching to the Go proxy in `claude_tap_plus`. Here's the complete context:\n\n## Problem\nWhen using the kimi upstream API, Claude Code sends multi-turn conversations where assistant messages with tool_calls are missing `reasoning_content`. Kimi requires this field and returns 400 errors: \"thinking is enabled but reasoning_content is missing in assistant tool call message at index N\".\n\nThe current Go proxy (`injectThinkingContent` in `internal/proxy/reverse.go:632-738`) only injects empty strings for both `reasoning_content` and the `thinking` block. This is a minimal fix but doesn't restore the actual reasoning_content from previous turns.\n\nA Python reference implementation exists that does full caching:\n1. Caches `reasoning_content` from API responses (both SSE and non-SSE)\n2. Restores actual cached reasoning_content into subsequent requests using multi-level cache lookup (full content+tool_calls key → tool_calls-only key → fallback to most recent)\n3. Only applies to kimi\n\n## Requirements\n- Replicate the Python proxy's reasoning_content caching logic in Go\n- Only activate when upstream is kimi (determined by profile/provider/target URL)\n- Don't apply for other providers (GLM, Anthropic, etc.)\n- Thread-safe cache (proxy handles concurrent requests)\n\n## Current Code Architecture\n\n### Key files:\n1. `internal/proxy/reverse.go` - Main proxy with `injectThinkingContent()` (lines 632-738), `serveHTTP()` (lines 112-263), `handleStreaming()` (lines 270-329), `handleNonStreaming()` (lines 336-403)\n2. `internal/config/profiles.go` - `ProfileConfig` struct with `Provider string` field\n3. `internal/config/resolve.go` - `ResolveTargetConfig()` returns `ResolvedConfig` with `BaseURL`, `Model`\n4. `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - Entry point, creates `ReverseProxy`, calls `SetModel()` and `SetFallbackConfig()`\n\n### Current `injectThinkingContent` behavior:\n- Called in `serveHTTP()` at line 149 (after model rewrite) and line 182 (after fallback model rewrite)\n- For every assistant message with tool_use blocks:\n  - Injects `{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\"}` into content array if missing\n  - Sets `msg[\"reasoning_content\"] = \"\"` if missing\n- Applies unconditionally to ALL upstreams\n\n### Current response handling:\n- `handleNonStreaming` (line 336): reads full response, parses JSON, writes trace\n- `handleStreaming` (line 270): SSE reassembler collects chunks, reconstructs full response, writes trace\n- Both have access to full response data including reasoning_content\n\n### Profile config:\n```json\n{\n  \"profiles\": {\n    \"kimi\": {\n      \"base_url\": \"https://api.kimi.com/coding\",\n      \"auth_token\": \"...\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"model\": \"kimi-for-coding\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### ResolvedConfig struct (from resolve.go):\n```go\ntype ResolvedConfig struct {\n    BaseURL    string\n    APIKey     string\n    AuthToken  string\n    Model      string\n}\n```\n\n### Python proxy cache key strategies:\n1. **Full key**: MD5 of (content + tool_calls JSON) - exact match\n2. **ToolCall key**: MD5 of (tool_calls JSON only) - for when content='' but tool_calls present\n3. **Fallback**: Most recently cached reasoning_content for any tool_call message\n\n### Python proxy cache sources:\n- **Non-SSE**: Extract `reasoning_content` from `response.choices[].message` \n- **SSE**: Accumulate `reasoning_content` from streaming delta chunks, cache at [DONE]\n\n## Design questions to address:\n1. Where should the cache live? (new struct? part of ReverseProxy?)\n2. How to determine \"is kimi\"? (check URL? add field to ResolvedConfig? add Provider field?)\n3. Should the existing `injectThinkingContent` be modified or replaced?\n4. How to extract reasoning_content from SSE responses (the reassembler accumulates it)?\n5. How to extract reasoning_content from non-SSE responses?\n6. Cache eviction strategy? (the Python proxy keeps everything in memory forever)\n7. How to handle the fallback case (when upstream switches from kimi to GLM)?\n\nPlease design a detailed, step-by-step implementation plan. Be specific about which functions to modify and which new functions/structs to create. Include the cache key strategy matching the Python proxy.","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_use_id":"call_7b56d0ea370241359e9098fd"}
